> A hand-checkable calculation

Sixteen independent unit-variance coordinates with mean shift1 give KL8 nats. Free-nats clipping belongs to the report objective; the native Kl calculation returns the unclipped value. This source uses an LSTM deterministic state.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/planet_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){std::filesystem::create_directories("build");dm::nn::ParameterStore p(0);dm::nn::models::Rssm m(p,{});dm::nn::models::RssmGauss q{dm::nn::ones({1,16}),dm::nn::zeros({1,16})},prior{dm::nn::zeros({1,16}),dm::nn::zeros({1,16})};std::vector<double>values{m.Kl(q,prior).item<double>()};std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");for(size_t i=0;i<values.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,values[i]);std::vector<double>x(values.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);double low=std::min(0.,*std::min_element(values.begin(),values.end())),high=std::max(0.,*std::max_element(values.begin(),values.end())),span=std::max(1.,high-low);dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(x,values,"computed values",{37,99,235}).ylim(low-.05*span,high+.05*span).title("planet worked calculation").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/planet_worked.svg");}
```
